<title>MALAYSIA: Bank Islam, Perfect suspended.</title>
<headline>Bank Islam, Perfect suspended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Trading in the shares of Bank Islam Malaysia Bhd and Perfect Food Industries Bhd were suspended on Thursday, a Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange official said.</p>
<p>She said the suspensions were on requests from the companies.</p>
<p>Officials of the company were not immediately available for comment.</p>
<p>Bank Islam Malaysia is the country's only islamic bank, while Perfect Food is a maker and distributor of snack food.</p>
<p>Bank Islam said on Wednesday that the government had asked it to take a lead role in the privatisation of the Finance Ministry's housing loan division.</p>
<p>Islamic banking operates according to the Sharia law, under which taking and paying interest is considered usury.</p>
<p>-- Kuala Lumpur newsroom (603-201 4813)</p>
